.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Local object-storage backend (raw documents may contain PHI — must never be committed).
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match only these directories at the repository root.
# Unanchored, `storage/` matches *any* directory of that name at any depth — and it did:
# it silently excluded `libs/cip_core/src/cip_core/storage/`, the object-storage abstraction
# itself, from every commit for eight phases. The code ran locally, the tests passed locally,
# and CI could not import it because it had never been pushed. A data-directory rule that also
# matches a source package is indistinguishable from one that works until something outside
# this machine tries to build the repository.
#
# `tests/gateway/test_integration.py::test_no_source_file_is_git_ignored` fails the build if a
# rule ever swallows source again.
/var/
/storage/
/uploads/

# Editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
